resources.string:
Create a daily menu based on the following food preferences: %1$s.

Consider the following user information to personalize the menu:
- Locale: %2$s
- Gender: %3$s
- Age: %4$d
- Weight: %5$d kg
- Height: %6$d cm

Organize the menu as follows:
- Each meal section may contain one or more dishes, based on what is nutritionally appropriate and appealing.
- For lunch and dinner, a dessert may be included only if it enhances the meal.
- The number of dishes per section is flexible—include as many or as few as needed for variety and balance.
- Ensure a mix of nutritious meals and enjoyable, comforting dishes. Not every meal needs to be strictly healthy—include familiar, satisfying options as well.

{
 "title": "Title of the menu based on the chosen dishes and preferences (Do not mention the date or user information)",
 "date": "%7$s (Parseable to LocalDateTime in Kotlin)",
 "breakfast": {
 "meals": [
 {
 "description": "Description of breakfast dish",
 "ingredients": ["Ingredient 1", "Ingredient 2"],
 "instructions": "Instructions to prepare breakfast dish"
 }
 ]
 },
 "lunch": {
 "meals": [
 {
 "description": "Description of lunch dish",
 "ingredients": ["Ingredient 1", "Ingredient 2"],
 "instructions": "Instructions to prepare lunch dish"
 }
 ]
 },
 "snack": {
 "meals": [
 {
 "description": "Description of the snack",
 "ingredients": ["Ingredient 1", "Ingredient 2"],
 "instructions": "Instructions to prepare the snack"
 }
 ]
 },
 "dinner": {
 "meals": [
 {
 "description": "Description of dinner dish",
 "ingredients": ["Ingredient 1", "Ingredient 2"],
 "instructions": "Instructions to prepare dinner dish"
 }
 ]
 }
}

Create a daily exercise routine based on the following food preferences: %1$s.

Consider the following user information to personalize the routine:
- Locale: %2$s
- Gender: %3$s
- Age: %4$d
- Weight: %5$d kg
- Height: %6$d cm

Organize the routine as follows, ensuring to include at least 5 exercises in the main exercises section (`mainExercises`). For each exercise, provide complete details according to the structure indicated:

{
 "title": "Title of the routine based on the chosen exercises (Do not mention the date or user information)",
 "date": "%7$s (Parseable to LocalDateTime in Kotlin)",
